# 02 - fading LED

## Objective

Control the brightness of an LED by gradually increasing and decreasing its intensity using PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) on the ESP32.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- LED
- 220 Ω resistor
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- PWM (Pulse Width Modulation)
- LEDC (ESP32 PWM)
- Duty cycle
- GPIO Output
- `ledcAttach()`
- `ledcWrite()`
- `for` loops
- Variables

## Wiring

- LED Anode → GPIO 23 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND

## Expected Result

The LED smoothly fades from off to full brightness, then fades back to off continuously.

## What I Learned

- How PWM controls LED brightness
- The difference between digital output and PWM output
- How duty cycle affects LED intensity
- How to use `for` loops for gradual changes
- How to configure PWM on the ESP32

## Challenges

- Configuring the correct PWM channel and output pin.
- Adjusting the delay values to achieve a smooth fading effect.

## Improvements

- Add a potentiometer to control the fade speed.
- Fade multiple LEDs simultaneously.
- Create different breathing light patterns.
- Control the brightness wirelessly using Bluetooth or Wi-Fi.

